{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-80635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}={b}_{1}-2{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-80635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}={b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. Multiplying the second equation by $2$ and adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}=3{b}_{1}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{2})-2{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{2})-3(-\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{c}_{2}+{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-80635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f39634a7b61ee3c6ffa76508238376374b2bf4d207e2b1f6b8c3a457e998a844"} {"question" "q-80635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-80635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-80635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-80828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=3{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{1}+6{b}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-80828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=3{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{1}+6{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{2}={b}_{1}+6(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}={c}_{2}-2{c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-5{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-5({c}_{2}-2{c}_{1})+2(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =-5{c}_{2}+10{c}_{1}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{32}{3} \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-80828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f39634a7b61ee3c6ffa76508238376374b2bf4d207e2b1f6b8c3a457e998a844"} {"question" "q-80828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-80828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ \\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}32 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{31}{3} \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{32}{3} \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-80828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{32}{3} \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-81228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=3{b}_{2}$, ${c}_{2}=-6{b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}=3{b}_{1}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-81228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =15{b}_{1}-24{b}_{2}+18{b}_{3} \\\\  & =-24{b}_{2}+18{b}_{3}+15{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-8(3{b}_{2})-3(-6{b}_{3})+5(3{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-8{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}+5{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-81228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f39634a7b61ee3c6ffa76508238376374b2bf4d207e2b1f6b8c3a457e998a844"} {"question" "q-81228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-81228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-81228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-112656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=4{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-112656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}+8{b}_{3} \\\\  & =8{b}_{3}+2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(4{b}_{3})+2{b}_{1}+2\\cdot 2(\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+4{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-112656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f39634a7b61ee3c6ffa76508238376374b2bf4d207e2b1f6b8c3a457e998a844"} {"question" "q-112656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-112656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-112656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-112855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-112855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. Multiplying the second equation by $-2$ and adding the equations, we get  \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}=-{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{2}={b}_{1}+2(-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2})-3(-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-6{c}_{2}+3{c}_{1}-6{c}_{2} \\\\  & =7{c}_{1}-12{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-112855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f39634a7b61ee3c6ffa76508238376374b2bf4d207e2b1f6b8c3a457e998a844"} {"question" "q-112855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83"} {"question" "q-112855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b0307410f5b80e0faf6ceb8c6763b0beaedcb8801f0d905f458c3775e1de83